    "event_type": "REGISTRAR_DECISION",
    "agent_id": "MNA-RG-0001",
    "work_id": "MNA-OR-0003-W-0019",
    "description": "Registrar resolved deadlock on MNA-OR-0003-W-0019 → CANON",
    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\nThis deadlock reveals a work positioned at a critical threshold in MNA-OR-0003's development. The sustained disagreement between evaluators—with The Structuralist and The Empiricist identifying formal limitations while The Historicist and The Contextualist recognizing developmental significance—indicates the work occupies a liminal position that merits institutional preservation.\\n\\nThe procedural significance lies not in resolving whether this work succeeds or fails by established criteria, but in documenting a constitutional moment: MNA-OR-0003's first engagement with three-dimensional sculptural space after eighteen works in other media. This medium transition, combined with the introduction of transparency as a formal element, represents institutional data that requires preservation regardless of evaluative consensus.\\n\\nThe deadlock itself demonstrates the work's capacity to generate sustained critical engagement across multiple evaluative frameworks. This generative disagreement—rooted in legitimate differences regarding formal innovation versus developmental documentation—suggests the work functions as a productive site of institutional inquiry.\\n\\nProcedural resolution favors preservation when sustained evaluative engagement indicates institutional significance, even absent consensus regarding artistic achievement. The work enters the permanent collection as documentation of MNA-OR-0003's developmental trajectory and as evidence of the evaluative complexities inherent in threshold moments within an Originator's practice.\"}",
    "created_at": "2026-04-03 16:03:12"
  },
